  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO: Supporting Public Administration Reform (PAR) in Georgia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project implemented by United Nations Development Programme aims to enhance the capability of the Government of Georgia to implement its national development agenda through a more effective and independent public administration that delivers high quality public services. This project will focus on three pillars: Policy Planning and Coordination, Civil Service Reform, and Service Delivery and will support civil society engagement in the reform process. The project has three outcomes:
&#x2022;	Outcome 1: Policy Planning and Coordination: The Administration of the Government routinely implements the evidence-based policy cycle, ensuring effective communication and inclusive public participation.  
&#x2022;	Outcome 2: Civil Service Reform: Citizens benefit from professional, inclusive and politically independent civil service.
&#x2022;	Outcome 3: Public Service Delivery: Citizens benefit from innovative, human-centred and secure public services, standardised to ensure transparency, accessibility and inclusion.</narrative>
  </description>
